/**
 * Imports contacts migrated from the legacy system.
 *
 * Migrated contacts are existing customers, so they must not get a welcome task. The import
 * bypasses only the TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask trigger action, using the Trigger Actions
 * Framework bypass API. All other Contact automation still runs, including
 * TA_Contact_FormatPhone.
 *
 * The bypass applies only to this method's single DML statement. It is removed in a finally
 * block, so it is cleared even when the insert fails. If the caller had already bypassed the
 * action before calling this method, that bypass is left in place.
 */
public with sharing class ContactImportService {

    /**
     * Inserts the given contacts in one DML statement, without creating welcome tasks.
     *
     * @param contacts the contacts to insert
     */
    public static void importContacts(List<Contact> contacts) {
        if (contacts == null || contacts.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Using the class reference instead of a string gives compile-time safety.
        System.Type welcomeTaskAction = TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask.class;

        // Record whether the caller already set this bypass, so we only clear what we set.
        Boolean wasAlreadyBypassed = MetadataTriggerHandler.isBypassed(welcomeTaskAction);
        if (!wasAlreadyBypassed) {
            MetadataTriggerHandler.bypass(welcomeTaskAction);
        }

        try {
            // One DML statement, in user mode so the running user's CRUD/FLS is enforced.
            insert as user contacts;
        } finally {
            if (!wasAlreadyBypassed) {
                MetadataTriggerHandler.clearBypass(welcomeTaskAction);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Notes:
- **Why after-insert is covered:** the after-insert actions run inside the same `insert` call, before it returns. So the bypass is active when `TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask` would run, and it is cleared straight afterwards.
- **Contacts inserted later:** they get their welcome task as normal, because the bypass is gone once the method returns.
- **Scope of the bypass:** only that one action is bypassed, using `MetadataTriggerHandler`'s action-level API. Contact as a whole is not bypassed (`TriggerBase.bypass`), so `TA_Contact_FormatPhone` and all other Contact automation still run.
- **User mode:** `insert as user` enforces CRUD and field-level security. If the migration runs as a user who lacks access to some Contact fields, the insert will fail. Grant that access, or switch to `insert contacts;` if this is a trusted system-level migration.

