Each piece of legacy logic now lives in its own action class, registered through custom metadata. Two choices are worth knowing before you read the files.

- **Bulk fix:** `TA_Case_AddClosureComment` collects every comment and inserts them all in one DML statement. Closing 200 cases uses one DML and no SOQL.
- **Sharing:** the classes are `with sharing`, which is stricter than the legacy trigger (it ran in system context). This should be safe because the user is already editing the Case. If some users can edit Cases but not create Case Comments, the closure-comment action would now fail for them; switch that one class to `inherited sharing` to restore the old behaviour exactly.

Nothing here has been deployed or tested; no test classes were requested, so none are included.

